# Cloud Build upload context for `gcloud run deploy --source .` (backend/).
# Without this file gcloud finds no .gcloudignore/.gitignore in backend/ and
# uploads EVERYTHING - .venv, node_modules (93MB workerd.exe), __pycache__ -
# bloating the context to ~200MB and making layer pushes slow/flaky
# (root cause of the 2026-09-07 ContainerImageImportFailed deploys).
# The Dockerfile only COPYs pyproject.toml, app/, alembic/, alembic.ini, so
# nothing here is needed in the image.
#
# SECRETS - MUST stay excluded. Because this .gcloudignore exists, gcloud stops
# consulting .gitignore, so .env is NOT auto-excluded here. The image is clean
# either way (the Dockerfile never COPYs .env), but `gcloud run deploy --source`
# uploads the whole source zip to a GCS bucket BEFORE the build - so a missing
# .env exclusion leaked real keys into that private bucket (security a5,
# 2026-09-07). Keep these first. (No `#!include:.gitignore`: backend/ has no
# .gitignore, and gcloud errors on a missing include.)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*-sa*.json
var/
.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.git/
tests/
data/
*.log
# Intermediate cert-curation scratch with non-ASCII (Korean) filenames.
# Already consolidated into certifications_curated.json and loaded from
# Firestore at runtime - no code reads these. Their non-UTF-8/Windows-encoded
# tar entry names make Cloud Run reject the image at import
# (ContainerImageImportFailed, 2026-09-07). Keep them in the repo, out of the image.
app/etl/seeds/cert_candidates_*
